-- title:
--   Moduli package at a supersingular point of the two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root with $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the modular function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ and with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi$, let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-function. Consider the two-chart integral model $\mathcal{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the spectra of the algebras of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathcal{X}$ at which the germ of the global function coming from $\varpi$ via the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a point of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y) = z$, such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$ the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with invertible discriminant and that $j$-invariant has no nonzero affine $q$-torsion point. Then there exist: a discrete valuation domain $A_0$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite, an $A_0$-algebra structure on $A$ with injective structure map making $A$ a finite $A_0$-module, an element $\zeta_A \in A$ mapping to $\zeta$ with $A = A_0[\zeta_A]$, with $\ell$ and $M'$ units in $A_0$; the equivariance data $h\ell$, $hM$, $hL$ (stability of the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point condition under variable change, of the condition `IsGamma0PowAt` under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`, and of divisibility of [`ModularCurve.inLineMulPoly`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassH1Pow.html#L18) under variable change); group laws $\mathcal{G}$ over $A_0$ that are chord-tangent and origin-identity, a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for $q$ that is a section transport, and families $hVC$, $hCO$ of graded variable-change and coefficient homomorphisms between projective Weierstrass model rings; a representing package $P_0$ of type `LevelModuliPackageAbs A₀ (rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓ M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯).toLevelModuliDatum`, whose coordinate ring $P_0.B_0$ is of finite type over $A_0$; a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $P_0.B_0$ containing the image of $q$ and supersingular in the same sense (every homomorphism to an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with kernel $\mathfrak{p}$ sends $P_0.j_0$ into [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7)); a ring isomorphism $\beta$ from the adic completion of the stalk of $\mathcal{X}$ at $z$ along its maximal ideal onto the $\mathfrak{p}$-adic completion of $P_0.B_0$; a ring homomorphism $\sigma_0 : A \to \widehat{(P_0.B_0)}_{\mathfrak{p}}$ agreeing on $A_0$ with the structure map; and proofs that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and that this element lies in the finite chart algebra. These are such that, first, for every $a \in A$ the image under $\beta$ of the germ at $z$ of the global function determined by $a$, viewed in the completion, equals $\sigma_0(a)$, and second, $\beta$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$, taken through the finite chart, of the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) to the image of $P_0.j_0$ in the $\mathfrak{p}$-adic completion.
--
--   This is the moduli-theoretic reading of a supersingular point on the two-chart integral model of the cyclotomic modular curve: the completed local ring of the geometric model at such a point is identified with the completed local ring of a finite-type algebra representing the rigidified level moduli problem with $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel data for $p \mid M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point and a Drinfeld $q$-level structure, compatibly with the base $A$ and with the $j$-coordinate. It feeds the subsequent analysis of that completed local ring as a regular local ring carrying an adic Drinfeld basis and Hasse parameter.
